CORE
test.c
--nondet-volatile-write-model reg:observe --mmio-weak --mmio-early-ack
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
the write has completed after the barrier: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
--
An inline-assembly ARM DMB (data memory barrier) is lowered to an ordering-only
fence, so under --mmio-early-ack it does not complete posted writes: the write
to reg may still be in flight after it and the completion assertion fails.
Compare dsb.desc. This demonstrates deriving the barrier semantics from source
(inline assembly) rather than a command-line flag.
